# Perturbation Harness

NEVER FOR PRODUCTION USE.

This module is the Phase 5 fault-injection surface (DEC-0012 #1/#7): it
sends fault signals (SIGSEGV, SIGSTOP, SIGKILL, SIGUSR2) at target PIDs and
records every action as a JSON-lines replay-log entry (schema:
`include/safety_crit/perturb/replay_log.hpp`). Like the DEC-0007 test-only
`destroy()` and the DEC-0012 #5 worker corruption hook, it must never be
reachable from a production control flow; the `safety-critical-ha perturb`
subcommand and this library exist for the Compose scenario scenarios S1/S2/
S3/S5/S6 (T-0029) and deterministic replay (T-0030).

Usage:

```
safety-critical-ha perturb <category> --target <pid> [--target2 <pid>] [--out <path>]
```

Categories: `crash`, `stall`, `recover-stall`, `corrupt`, `double-fault`,
`supervisor-kill`. Records append to `--out` (default stdout).
